  "note": "Triennial election of the Portstewart Urban Council, polled Monday 15 May 1939. There was no contest: twelve candidates were nominated for the twelve seats (Belfast News-Letter, 6 May 1939, p. 9). Newcomers were Messrs. M'Cutcheon, Herbert J. Black (a former member of Portrush U.D.C.) and Samuel Macfarlane. Of the retiring Council Messrs. J. M. C. Montagu, D.L., and W. Moody did not seek re-election. Returned unopposed."
